.TH WAIT_IFEXITED 3
.SH NAME
wait_ifexited \- check whether a wait status reports normal exit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "wait.h"
.PP
.BI "int wait_ifexited(int " wstat ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wait_ifexited
reports whether
.IR wstat ,
a status previously filled in by
.BR wait_pid (3),
.BR wait_nointr (3),
.BR wait_nohang (3),
.BR wait_pid_nohang (3),
or the
.I *pids
variants, describes a process that terminated normally (as opposed to
being killed by a signal). Portable across platforms: on WINDOWS_NATIVE
this is always true by the time a caller has
.IR wstat ,
since
.BR wait_pid (3)
and
.BR wait_pid_nohang (3)
already filter out the still-running case themselves -- callers should
use this instead of the POSIX
.B WIFEXITED()
macro to stay portable.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Nonzero if the process exited normally, 0 otherwise.
.SH SEE ALSO
wait_exitstatus(3), wait_pid(3)
